<title>FRANCE: Paribas confirms sold Canal Plus stake.</title>
<headline>Paribas confirms sold Canal Plus stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>French investment bank Societe Financiere de Paribas on Wednesday confirmed that it had sold a 1.33 percent stake in Canal Plus on Friday.</p>
<p>Belgian's Groupe Bruxelles Lambert GBL, controlled by businessman Albert Frere and a main shareholder on Luxembourg's Compagnie Luxembourgeoise de Telediffusion (CLT), has said it was the buyer.</p>
<p>Paribas said it had obtained its Canal Plus shares recently when it swapped its stake in broadcast rights company UGC DA for Canal Plus shares as part of a buy-out offer.</p>
</text>
